{
  "engine": "overtime/occurrence-pricing",
  "rateSet": "structural-fiction-v1",
  "_readme": [
    "Structural vectors (ADR-0018 §3): rate-independent logic only, computed against the",
    "deliberately fictional rate set in structural-fiction-v1.ts — every factor is 2.00,",
    "so nothing here is or resembles Indonesian regulation. Because the factor is uniform,",
    "the total cannot distinguish a wrong tier split from a right one: the `tiers` trace is",
    "the assertion that matters in every vector.",
    "A failing vector is a code defect until a human re-verifies the vector and records why",
    "it changed; a vector is never edited to make a test pass (testing-strategy §6.1).",
    "Input fields mirror OvertimePricingInput minus `rules` (injected by the runner from the",
    "declared rateSet). Minutes are integers; H = scheduledStandardMinutes, falling back to",
    "fallbackStandardDayMinutes when the schedule carries zero (BR-OVT-010)."
  ],
  "vectors": [
    {
